<%# locals: (reason: nil) %>
<%# The empty state of a FILTERED list: which filter emptied it, and the way back
    out (S3 of the filter-line plan, finding F5).

    The list carries up to seven filters at once and two of them are DEFAULTS
    nobody chose -- this month, and billed hidden -- so "Deine Filter haben keine
    Treffer ergeben" asked the reader to guess which of seven to touch, including
    two they never set.

    `reason` comes from TimeSessions::EmptyReason and is nil on the one path that
    renders this table without running the diagnosis (create.turbo_stream, whose
    list is unfiltered anyway); the generic sentence is what is left then.

    The reset stands whenever the diagnosis ran and no pill can help: no single
    filter explains the emptiness, or nothing removable narrows at all and the
    base itself is empty, which is a smart folder. It leads to the NEUTRAL list
    (all time, all three states), not to the bare address: the bare address
    re-applies the two defaults, and in the very case this branch exists for
    (the only booking is old AND billed) that is the same empty page again.

    The links carry turbo_frame: _top on purpose. The pills, the period segments
    and the selects all sit OUTSIDE time_sessions_list_frame, so a frame
    navigation would drop a filter from the list and leave it standing in the
    row above it. %>
<%
  culprits = reason&.culprits.presence
  removable = reason&.active.presence
  scope = 'views.organisations.time_sessions.empty_reason'
  # Everything the labels print, from ONE owner
  # (TimeSessionsController#build_filter_state), shared with the filter line and
  # the mobile badge since S7. A nil record is a name the reader may not read,
  # and the label falls back to the bare filter name.
  filter_state = @filter_state
  description = if culprits
                  t("#{scope}.culprits", count: culprits.size)
                elsif removable
                  t("#{scope}.none_alone")
                else
                  t('views.organisations.time_sessions.index_table.empty_no_results_description')
                end
%>

<% actions = capture do %>
  <% if culprits %>
    <% culprits.each do |key| %>
      <%= link_to time_filter_removal_url(key),
                  data: { turbo_frame: '_top', empty_filter: key },
                  class: TimeSessionsHelper::REMOVAL_CHIP_CLASSES do %>
        <i class="bi bi-x-lg text-[11px]" aria-hidden="true"></i>
        <%# Capped and clipped: a ticket or meeting title goes into this label,
            and a long one would stretch the pill across the card. %>
        <span class="max-w-[18rem] truncate"><%= time_filter_removal_label(key, filter_state) %></span>
        <%# The glyph says "remove" to a mouse and nothing at all to a screen
            reader, so the word travels with it. %>
        <span class="sr-only"><%= t("#{scope}.remove") %></span>
      <% end %>
    <% end %>
  <% elsif reason %>
    <%= link_to time_list_path(current_organisation, **TimeSession::LIST_NEUTRAL_DRILLDOWN_PARAMS),
                data: { turbo_frame: '_top', empty_reset: true },
                class: TimeSessionsHelper::REMOVAL_CHIP_CLASSES do %>
      <i class="bi bi-arrow-counterclockwise text-[11px]" aria-hidden="true"></i>
      <span><%= t("#{scope}.reset") %></span>
    <% end %>
  <% end %>
<% end %>

<div class="flex items-center justify-center min-h-[50vh]">
  <%= render 'shared/empty_content',
      variant: :no_results,
      icon_class: 'bi bi-search',
      title: t('views.organisations.time_sessions.index_table.empty_no_results_title'),
      description: description,
      actions: actions %>
</div>
